# TASK 4.1 memcheck: the config graph built by read_config (profiles,
# servers, peers) is process-lifetime ownership -- production frees card
# lists on reload and never tears the profile graph down outside process
# exit, and the unit harness parses once and exits. LSan stacks rooted in
# read_config are therefore retained-by-design, not lost. Any leak whose
# stack does NOT pass through read_config still reports normally.
leak:read_config
